  "details": "Firstly, compression is NOT the same as volume. If you're confused about the terminology, just watch the video here. https://youtu.be/LGqDVhww-hs\n\nSecond, I'm not talking about the audio bitrate. That's a different kind of the word \"compression\".\n\nEvery time when I talked to someone, I find myself adjusting individual's volume all the time because some are too quiet and some are too loud. VRChat implementation audio compressor solved this issue, but sometimes I wanted to turn that off or adjust it to be a little bit less aggressive. For the video recording and other reasons.\n\nVRChat implementation of compressing voice makes the quiet sound become very loud, like whispering become a shouting. My friends always pointing at me that my mic is too loud, but I've used the same mic as my Discord call, it sounds normal. I always check my mic level using VoiceMeeter software, and I need to adjust it to -12 dBFS (Decibels relative to full scale) all the time when I'm in VRChat. And goes back to 0 dBFS for Discord call and recording.\n\nI also lower my game audio to -14 dBFS on my mixer. Because of the aggressive compressor, the loudness of the voice become uncontrollably loud. Even if the audio is not peaking. \n\nMy speculation is maybe too much (too aggressive) threshold and ratio settings. I wish there's a way to adjust that myself, or just have a better default adjustment for everyone. And for the simplicity, most people might not know about how audio compressor work, maybe put that option behind advance audio settings or maybe in the config files.\n\nDiscord, for example, has the higher quality than VRChat's voice call system. Because they have less aggressive compressor settings, and other software to take note is Mumble, They let the user tinkle with compressor and limiter settings.",
